      "title": "Switching carriers midyear",
      "narration": "Priya moves her group to a new insurer on July 1. Without protection, her employees would face a second deductible in one year. A deductible carryover, or transfer of credit, provision counts expenses applied to the old plan’s deductible toward the new plan’s deductible for the rest of the year, and the same for coinsurance toward the out-of-pocket maximum. The no-loss no-gain rule requires the new carrier to cover employees as the old plan would have, including those currently disabled or hospitalized, so no one loses coverage because of the change and no one gains benefits they lacked before.",
